      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to understand the geometry of the semicircles and the areas involved in the shaded region.\n\n1. **Identify the radii:**\n   - The radius of each sector (arc \\(ADB\\), arc \\(BEC\\), and arc \\(DFE\\)) is given as 1 unit.\n   - The radius of the semicircle formed by arc \\(DFE\\) (let's call it \\(r_F\\)) is also 1 unit, because it is an excircle of the quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\) and similarly to \\(D\\) and \\(E\\).\n\n2. **Determine the area of each semicircle:**\n   - The area of a full circle with radius 1 unit is \\(\\pi \\times 1^2 = \\pi\\) square units.\n   - Since arc \\(ADB\\) and arc \\(BEC\\) are semicircles, each has an area of \\(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) square units.\n   - The area of arc \\(DFE\\) (the segment) is the area of the full circle minus the area of its semicircle: \\(\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) square units.\n\n3. **Calculate the area of the shaded region:**\n   - The shaded region consists of the areas of two semicircles (one full \\(ADB\\) and one full \\(BEC\\)) minus the area of one semicircle (arc \\(DFE\\)).\n   - Therefore, the area of the shaded region is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Include the right triangles:**\n   - Each of the right triangles \\(ADF\\), \\(DFE\\), \\(EBF\\) are each half of a right triangle with base 1 and height 1. So each unit triangle has area \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\frac{1}{2}\\).\n   - There are five such triangles in total, and since each triangle is covered once in the shaded area (as the shaded region actually includes three sides of these triangles), the area of the triangle is covered five times.\n   - Therefore, the area covered by the triangles is \\(5 \\times \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{5}{2}\\).\n\n5. **Total shaded area including triangles:**\n   - Sum of the area of the areas of the semicircles minus the area of the triangles:\n     \\[\n     \\left(\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) + \\frac{5}{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\frac{5}{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\frac{5}{2} = \\frac{\\pi + 5}{2}\n     \\]\n\n6. **Conclusion:**\n   - After subtracting one half the base and height triangles from the radius of the circle is half of the reduction of 2 radians coverage to 0.7 radians when subtracting the top, the final answer is:\n   The shaded area of the given region is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
